+# Bug Fix: Product stock consistency across cart, checkout, cancellation, and API availability
+
+- **Slug**: ticket
+- **Fixed**: 2026-11-18T00:00:00Z
+- **Assessment**: ./assessment.md
+- **Status**: applied
+
+## Summary
+
+Stock operations now use the ordered product SKU and the default (`*`) availability record. Cart and checkout paths reject insufficient quantities before persistence, product responses hide zero-stock items, and cancellation restores stock once while preventing later status changes.
+
+## Changes
+
+| File | Change | Notes |
+|------|--------|-------|
+| `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/order/OrderServiceImpl.java` | modified | Corrected product lookup and made inventory mismatch fail instead of logging. |
+| `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/shoppingCart/facade/ShoppingCartFacadeImpl.java` | modified | Validates cart stock for add, single update, and multi-update; uses default stock record. |
+| `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/order/facade/OrderFacadeImpl.java` | modified | Validates checkout stock, restores stock on cancellation, and rejects post-cancel status changes. |
+| `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/order/OrderApi.java` | modified | Preserves conflict exceptions for authenticated checkout. |
+| `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/shoppingCart/ShoppingCartApi.java` | modified | Preserves conflict exceptions for cart operations. |
+| `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/exception/ConflictRuntimeException.java` | added | Dedicated 409 exception. |
+| `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/exception/RestErrorHandler.java` | modified | Maps stock/status conflicts to HTTP 409. |
+| `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/populator/catalog/ReadableProductPopulator.java` | modified | Makes zero stock set `available` and `canBePurchased` false. |
+
+## Tests Added or Updated
+
+- No new automated test class was added; verification used the Maven compile check and existing project test command in the next phase.
+
+## Local Verification
+
+- Commands run: `mvn -q -DskipTests compile` → passed.
+- Manual checks: inspected the changed checkout, cart, status, exception, and product-population paths.
+
+## Deviations from Assessment
+
+The implementation uses the existing default-region (`*`) availability record as the authoritative stock source, matching the product API’s stock convention, rather than introducing a new inventory service or database locking layer.
+
+## Follow-ups
+
+- Add focused integration tests for HTTP 409 responses and concurrent checkout locking when a test fixture/database is available.
